@startuml
title Applying the empirical rule to a roulette simulation (MIT 6.0002 lecture 6)
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #EAF6F0
  BorderColor #2E8B67
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #2E8B67
}
start
:choose a game (Fair, European, American)
and a trial size numSpins;
repeat
  :play one trial: numSpins spins,
  bet 1 on pocket 2 every spin;
  :record the mean return per spin of the trial;
repeat while (fewer than 20 trials?) is (yes)
-> no;
:mean, std = getMeanAndStd(trial returns);
:report mean +/- 1.96 x std
"with 95 % confidence";<<#FFFFFF>>
note right
  1.96 x std is the spread of one trial's return.
  The uncertainty of the mean of 20 trials is
  smaller by sqrt(20): the standard error, lecture 7.
end note
:increase numSpins (1,000 -> 100,000 -> 1,000,000)
and observe the interval shrink as 1 / sqrt(numSpins);
stop
@enduml
